WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:03.300
A manuscript page fills with handwriting.

2
00:00:03.350 --> 00:00:08.930
Then one word lifts off the page
and turns to face you: Reader.

3
00:00:08.980 --> 00:00:10.110
"Who blames me?"

4
00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:11.390
she asks.

5
00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:14.670
Again and again, the word comes closer.

6
00:00:14.720 --> 00:00:18.870
And near the very end comes the
most famous line in the book.

7
00:00:18.920 --> 00:00:21.830
So why does Jane keep talking to you?

8
00:00:21.880 --> 00:00:26.420
In this mission, you'll meet two
Janes: the child who lives the story,

9
00:00:26.470 --> 00:00:28.990
and the adult telling it years later.

10
00:00:29.040 --> 00:00:32.560
You'll find out why the
novel appeared in 1847,

11
00:00:32.610 --> 00:00:35.680
"edited by" a mysterious Currer Bell.

12
00:00:35.730 --> 00:00:39.430
And you'll discover she turns
to you over thirty times.

13
00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:43.310
Your mission: explain why
Jane keeps talking to you.
